# Brand Kit collection profiles

**Collection** (UI) = `BargainingUnit` (code). Brand Kit profiles are *comms identities* (local number + sub-text + optional code), not Hub tenancy. A steward can speak for more than one workplace without changing colours or logo.

Companion research: [`docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-08-17-brand-kit-collections.md`](../../docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-08-17-brand-kit-collections.md).

## Product rules

1. **Do not assume FT/PT for every union.** That split is required for OPSEU CAAT Support under the *Colleges Collective Bargaining Act* — it is not a CUPE/Unifor/ONA/PSAC/USW default.
2. **Fresh Brand Kit / Other / non-OPSEU presets:** one **Local** profile. Hide the switcher until the steward adds a second collection.
3. **OPSEU preset only:** two collections — **College Support Full-time** (`ft`) and **College Support Part-time** (`pt`). Official sector names, not “Support Staff” for the whole union.
4. **Applying a preset replaces profiles.** Switching Unifor → OPSEU must not leave CAAT labels behind, and the reverse must not leave FT/PT on a CUPE kit.
5. **Saved kits are not rewritten on hydrate.** Existing localStorage FT/PT rows stay until the steward resets or re-applies a preset.
6. **Any union can add collections.** Amalgamated / multi-unit locals add named workplaces themselves. Do not hardcode a second union’s unit list into core defaults.
7. **No union names in generic chrome.** Copy talks about collections, workplaces, or units — not “full-time and part-time” unless the OPSEU CAAT labels are the stored data.

