## Default labels (Brand Kit)

| Preset | `#` | Stored labels | Code |
|---|---|---|---|
| *(none)* / Other / CUPE / Unifor / USW / ONA / PSAC | 1 | Local | — |
| `opseu` | 2 | College Support Full-time / College Support Part-time | `ft` / `pt` |

OPSEU stretch (do **not** default; offer only if a steward adds them): CAAT Academic FT + PT/Sessional; OPS Unified + Correctional; hospital / LTC / municipal as one collection per local.

## Sourced structures (do not flatten)

### OPSEU/SEFPO

Ontario colleges have **four** province-wide groups (CEC + OPSEU). Reference tenant is **CAAT Support** only.

- CAAT-S FT / College Support Full-time — [opseu.org/sector/college-support-full-time](https://opseu.org/sector/college-support-full-time)
- CAAT-S PT / College Support Part-time — [opseu.org/sector/college-support-part-time](https://opseu.org/sector/college-support-part-time)
- FT vs PT **must** be separate units under the *Colleges Collective Bargaining Act* — [OPSEU PT certification (2016)](https://opseu.org/news/opseu-applies-to-represent-part-time-college-support-staff/14462/)
- CEC: [FT Support](https://www.collegeemployercouncil.ca/bargaining/full-time_support_staff_2025), [PT Support](https://www.collegeemployercouncil.ca/bargaining/part-time-support-staff-bargaining) (also CAAT-A FT and CAAT-A PT/SL)
- Hours: FT support regularly **>24 hrs/week**; PT **≤24** — [OPSEU Local 137](https://opseu137.ca/opseu-local-137)
- College locals are composite (Academic local + Support local; each with FT + PT) — [CAAT-A intro (Local 562 PDF)](https://www.opseu562.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Intro-to-CAAT-A-2025.pdf)
- ~500 local units / 17 sectors — [Local 2100 structure](https://opseu2100.ca/organization/structure-governance/), [Owners’ Manual PDF](https://opseu5121.ca/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/opseu-orientation-booklet-2020.pdf)
- Central CAs: [Find your collective agreement](https://opseu.org/information/general/find-your-collective-agreement/12967/)

### CUPE

Employer- and history-specific. **Default one Local.** Examples only:

- One local, several units (U of T 3261) — [cupe.ca coordinated bargaining](https://cupe.ca/counterpoint/three-locals-one-goal-how-coordination-transformed-their-bargaining-strategy)
- ~230 PSE units — [Sector profile: Post-Secondary](https://cupe.ca/sector-profile-post-secondary)
- Local 2484 ~20 child-care units — [Raising the floor](https://cupe.ca/raising-floor-child-care-workers)
- Toronto Local 79: FT, Unit B PT, Recreation PT, LTC PT — [City of Toronto settlement PDF](https://www.toronto.ca/legdocs/mmis/2020/cc/bgrd/backgroundfile-148172.pdf)
- OLRB may order FT+PT **or** all-employee — [Loyalist Township 1998](https://www.minicounsel.ca/olrb/1998/18288), [Kawartha Pine Ridge 1998](https://www.minicounsel.ca/olrb/1998/m125)

### Unifor

Single-unit **or** amalgamated (2+ bargaining units). ~40% amalgamated locals / ~80% of members.

- [Guide to Amalgamated Local Unions (PDF)](https://www.unifor.org/sites/default/files/legacy/documents/document/unifor-amalgamatedlocals-en.pdf)
- [Servicing bargaining units (PDF)](https://www.unifor.org/sites/default/files/legacy/documents/document/unifor-servicingbargainingunits-en-print.pdf)
- [Constitution 2023 (PDF)](https://www.unifor.org/sites/default/files/documents/Unifor%20Constitution%202023.pdf)

Default **Local**. Amalgamated stewards add one profile per unit they comms for.

### USW

Amalgamated locals + **units** (unit chair). ~37% amalgamated locals / ~65% of members (international figure).

- [Resolution 17: Amalgamation](https://usw.org/usw-convention/resolution-no-17-amalgamation/)
- [USW Local 1998 — 7 units, each with a CA](https://www.usw1998.ca/union-101/)
- [Local 1944 units](https://usw1944.ca/function)
- [USW Canada — new unit inside amalgamated local](https://usw.ca/security-guards-vale-join-steelworkers/)

Default **Local**. Extra profiles = unit / workplace names.

### ONA

Local = 1+ **employer bargaining units** (not usually FT/PT). 60+ Locals, 500+ BUs.

- [Regions, Locals & Bargaining Units](https://ona.org/regions-locals-bargaining-units/)
- [How bargaining works](https://ona.org/how-bargaining-works/) (central + local agreement)
- [Constitution (PDF)](https://ona.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/ona_statementofbeliefsconstitution_20260102.pdf)

Default **Local**. Multi-BU locals add a profile per employer/site they comms for.

### PSAC

Locals → Components (or Directly Chartered Locals). Bargaining units are **employer + classification**, not FT/PT.

- [Our structure](https://psacunion.ca/our-structure-1)
- [Which bargaining unit am I in?](https://psacunion.ca/which-bargaining-unit-am-i-in) (Treasury Board PA / TC / EB / SV)
- [Bargaining overview](https://psacunion.ca/bargaining-0)

Default **Local**. Optional extra profiles: PA, CRA, workplace name.

## Do not

- Ship CUPE/Unifor/USW/ONA/PSAC unit lists as hardcoded Brand Kit defaults
- Treat Collection profiles as Hub `bargainingUnitId` tenancy
- Reintroduce CAAT FT/PT as `DEFAULT_BRAND_KIT` for every first visit
- Bundle another union’s official marks because OPSEU has a reference pack — see [`session-knowledge-2026-07-30-multi-union-sources.md`](../../docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-07-30-multi-union-sources.md)
